// So uhh I tried to figure out pest files and that went horribly.
// Its been a bit since I had to use awk in any capacity, and Im pretty tired so its not sticking
// But, fortunately, pest is a good language. This exercise, even though it doesn't compile, reveals a lot of structure that I can use. 

// Since rust pest crate is basically just a codegen package, I can achieve the same result by just writing out the grammar by hand,
// and I can probably do that faster than I can figure out this pretentious ass system.

// thus, the ".fakepest" file. It's authoritative if your faith stat is high enough. I'll probably revisit later, but I'm tired tonight.

Program = _{SOI ~ ("\n"+)* ~ Comment* ~ Object* ~ EOI}

Object = {Field+}

WHITESPACE = _{"[ \t\f]+"}

Text = {"[^%>\n: ][^%:\n]*"}

KeyValueSeparator = {":"}

Separator = {"\n"}

ConnectionDirective = {">"}

Comment = _{"%" ~ Text}

KeyValueField = {Text ~ KeyValueSeparator ~ Text}

UnlabeledField = {Text}

ConnectionField = {ConnectionDirective ~ Text}

Field = {KeyValueField | UnlabaledField | ConnectionField ~ LineComment? ~ Separator}